\section{Carry Remembered Edges Across Evacuation}

\begin{verbatim}
write_reference(holder, slot, value):
    slot.store(value)
    if in_old(holder) and in_current_young(value):
        dirty(card_containing(slot))

collect_young():
    stop_mutators_with_completed_barriers()
    old_cards := snapshot_dirty_cards()
    next_cards := empty_card_set()
    for slot in roots:
        slot.store(evacuate_if_young(slot.load()))
    for slot in unique_pointer_slots_on(old_cards):
        slot.store(evacuate_if_young(slot.load()))
        if in_survivor_young(slot.load()):
            next_cards.add(card_containing(slot))
    while evacuation_queue not empty:
        holder := evacuation_queue.pop()
        for slot in strong_slots(holder):
            slot.store(evacuate_if_young(slot.load()))
            if in_old(holder) and in_survivor_young(slot.load()):
                next_cards.add(card_containing(slot))
    finish_flip_and_install(next_cards)
\end{verbatim}

This example uses a stop-the-world copying nursery with an
old region that is not moved by the minor cycle.
\texttt{evacuate\_if\_young} tests the old nursery range; it
copies once and queues objects whether they land in young
survivor space or are promoted. The pseudocode maintains a
fresh set rather than clearing every dirty card after it
is read. If a surviving old-to-young edge stays in place
and no mutator rewrites it, clearing its card would lose it
at the next minor collection. Likewise, a freshly promoted
object can acquire old-to-young edges even without any
mutator store. The evacuation scan must account for them.

\section{Scan Precisely Inside Coarse Cards}

A card is an address range, not a sequence of tagged values.
The first bytes may be the tail of an object that starts on
an earlier card. Find that object using an object-start or
block-offset structure, then consult its descriptor for
reference slots in the dirty card. If instead the implementation
marks a holder's starting card, its scanner must enumerate
all fields of the holder, not just those physically on that
card. A large reference array crossing a boundary with its
only young value in the final slot distinguishes these two
interpretations. Store and scanner must use the same one.

An unchecked store in an initialization helper is not
automatically safe. It may initialize an old object allocated
directly into the old region. Likewise, a vector copy, a
native setter, and generated code specialized for a known
shape may bypass a generic setter. Check every operation
that can write a reference, and give bulk stores a documented
way to mark the affected ranges before reaching a safepoint.
In the simple cooperative protocol, no pause can occur
between the store and its post-barrier; concurrent collection
requires a stricter protocol for publication and cleaning.

\section{Tune Using Survival and Scan Cost}

An age threshold counts completed young survivals, not wall
time. Promoting quickly reduces repeated copying but puts
more data beyond the reach of minor reclamation. If a workload
keeps objects alive for three minor pauses and discards them
before the fourth, a threshold of two tends to promote
objects that die soon thereafter. Increasing the nursery can
reduce the number of times these objects are seen, but also
raises the maximum live volume and changes pause distribution.
Track copied bytes by age, promotion bytes, and occupancy
of the destination before changing thresholds.

Repeated updates to a wide old table can spread dirty cards
over much of old space. Then a nominally minor cycle spends
more time scanning old memory than its name suggests. Measure
dirty card count, bytes of old storage examined, and actual
old-to-young slots found. Sparse referents over densely dirty
cards might justify refinement or a different card size;
a single highly reused card may be cheaper than an exact
set with many duplicate insertion attempts.

\section{Test What the Young Collector Deliberately Ignores}

Force two minor collections with no intervening store to
the old queue, inspect the request through that queue after
both, then clear the slot and check that the request can
die. Test a promotion whose child remains young. In debug
builds, compare the remembered coverage against a walk of
all old reference slots before invoking a minor cycle.
Presence of additional dirty cards is acceptable; absence of
one actual incoming slot is not. Finally include garbage
old objects whose fields retain young ones. The minor policy
may keep those young objects alive until an old or full
cycle proves their holders dead. That conservative retention
is a cost of collecting only part of the heap, not a reason
to ignore such fields at the next minor cycle.

\section{Reserve Space for a Promotion Spike}

Suppose the nursery has 8 MiB occupied, only 3 MiB of young
survivor space is free, and old space can accept another 1 MiB.
If 5 MiB turns out to survive, neither the age threshold nor
the three-region layout guarantees a destination. A runtime
can reserve enough destination space before the pause, grow
the allowed destination, or implement a promotion-failure
fallback with explicit metadata. A naive fallback restarts
marking at the old roots and walks the old nursery exactly as
before. That is not valid after forwarding has destroyed some
headers and roots and fields point into both destinations.
Fault-inject at every allocation used by evacuation to ensure
the chosen policy cannot silently enter that state.

A full cycle that moves old objects also affects remembered
state. With an exact remembered set, the address of a slot may
change even though the referent remains young. In a card
table, moving a holder to a new card invalidates the old card
as a description of that edge. Rebuild the remembered set
during full tracing or demonstrate that the full cycle leaves
no young survivors. For a test, move a holder while keeping a
young referent, run a minor cycle without rewriting the holder,
and verify that the relocated holder still names the referent.
Testing only the full collection would miss this failure.
Verify the same boundary when a full cycle reclassifies a
young region as old without changing any addresses. Generation
membership, not address stability, determines which stores
must be represented in the remembered set.
